WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.120
Daddy [Dupuy Anderson] filed suit to integrate LSU. . . The students at Lee High and . . . Most of the high school students,

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:13.720
white high school students, think LSU is heaven, and when they found out . . . they were enraged: “Oh, the nigger thinks she’s smart.

3
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:14.980
She can go to LSU now.

4
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.260
It wasn’t good enough to just integrate the public schools, now she’s going to LSU.

5
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.460
We’ve got to have these coons out at LSU.”

6
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.780
All of this crap all over again.

7
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:31.280
So graduating from Lee High didn’t mean anything to me because I knew I had to go through this stuff all over again . . .

8
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.640
After all of that at Lee High, why did you decide to go to LSU?

9
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.680
I was on a mission then.

10
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.940
It was just a point to prove.

11
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.480
You had to go on with it.

12
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.820
If I could survive Lee High, I could survive anything.

13
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.080
So it wasn’t, it wasn’t fear of anything or . . . I mean,

14
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.480
I was just so hard by that time, it just didn’t make me any difference . . .

15
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.440
As Daddy kept saying, he said, “My children don’t have to do this.”

16
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.260
He said, “Because I can send them anywhere I want to.”

17
00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:03.160
He said, “I’m hoping that we’re opening doors for children that can’t afford to do this, whose only choice might be LSU.”

18
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.080
So, that’s what I thought that we were doing.

19
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:13.560
I was hoping that we were pioneering the way to open the doors for students that would only have this as an alternative,

20
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.460
that had, just did not have any other option.

21
00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:22.040
That hopefully with an equal educational system, if we were at LSU then maybe they would equalize the facilities at Southern.

22
00:01:22.040 --> 00:02:31.300
We just kept saying equal.

23
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:37.900
The guy from Shreveport spent a lot of time with us because he was living on campus.

24
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.380
They trashed his dorm.

25
00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.560
They broke the windows in the dorm.

26
00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:49.140
The police had to come and protect him one night when they started throwing bricks and things through the windows of the dorm.

27
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.480
I don’t know if that ever made the paper or not . . .

28
00:02:52.480 --> 00:03:01.160
. . . The Ku Klux Klan came out and burned a cross in front of the library one night about two weeks after we had been in school.

29
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:06.400
The next morning when we arrived at school the cross was just laying down on the ground in front of the library.

30
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.260
The students erected the cross again during the day: “Niggers go home.”

31
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:18.840
It’s so ridiculous because A. P. Tureaud, Jr.[sic] had already integrated the law school, so there were blacks on campus in the law school.

32
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.200
Then they had to file suit again and integrate the graduate school at LSU.

33
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.200
So there were grad students on campus at LSU.

34
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.600
Then, we had to file suit again to integrate the undergrad.

35
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:37.460
I’m willing to bet that LSU is the only university in the country that had three separate suits filed to integrate each division.

36
00:03:37.460 --> 00:04:30.240
I know of no other.

37
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:39.520
How much of what you did do you feel the younger people coming up right behind you knew of what you did? . . .

38
00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.240
They didn’t know.

39
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:48.460
Again, as I said, Baton Rouge kept everything quiet, so nobody really knew what we were going through.

40
00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:54.300
The adults didn’t know what we were going through, let alone the kids . . . They weren’t forewarned,

41
00:04:54.300 --> 00:05:03.860
and it was almost as if each generation that began to come in had to go through it all over again.

42
00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:11.760
It wasn’t as severe as what we went through, but they would, every class was breaking ground again.

43
00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:15.740
With each new class that came in, every freshman class.
